# Repo-wide line-ending policy.
#
# Everything here is consumed by shells and editors that are unforgiving about
# carriage returns: a CRLF .vimrc fails on every line under Unix vim, CRLF
# breaks PowerShell here-strings, and `sh` chokes on `\r` at the end of a
# command. So: normalise to LF in the index AND check out LF on every
# platform, including Windows, regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# text=auto still lets git detect binaries and leave them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where CRLF is actively harmful.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=lf
*.psm1      text eol=lf
*.psd1      text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never touch these.
*.dll       binary
*.pdb       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
